# Openings' step 2s that run through talk (docs/DESIGN.md, "Openings"; Guidance/RZ_OpeningSteps.c). The
# character flag opening.task is step 2's task (RZ_EOpeningTask: 10 the open channel, 16 the two
# families), opening.step the step under way. The step's clock runs once the flag below is set:
# opening.settled (1 settled, 2 half settled), opening.answered (1 answered). Voice: plain.

conv opening.settle
for opening
when cflag:opening.step=2 & cflag:opening.task=16 & cflag:opening.settled=0
topic "All right. What's the trouble?"
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say The Kerns and the Orlovs share the coal shed out the back. The Kerns say the Orlovs took the last of it in the night. The Orlovs say it was theirs, and the Kerns' boy kicked their dog.
  say Nobody's lying, which is the trouble. They've stopped speaking, and it's cold at night. They'll listen to you. Say something they can both live with.
  > @split Split the coal, and the boy says sorry. -> settled | half | half   check persuade none 1 bg:elder do cset:opening.settled=1 short cset:opening.settled=2 else cset:opening.settled=2
  > @later Let me think on it. -> hub

node settled
  say Old Kern laughed. Nobody's heard him laugh since the roads shut. The Orlov girl is fetching the dog to be apologised to, and there's a kettle on in both houses.
  > @good Good. Tell them I said so. -> hub

node half
  say They heard you. They didn't like it. They'll take turns with the coal and not look at each other on the stairs. It'll do until somebody's colder.
  > @enough That'll have to do for now. -> hub

conv opening.channel
for radio:open
when cflag:opening.step=2 & cflag:opening.task=10 & cflag:opening.answered=0
topic "I hear you. Who's calling?"
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say Anyone at all, on this. I've been calling since it got light. I'm in a house on my own with the shutters down and a radio, and nobody's answered. Just say you're there. I don't need anything else.
  > @here I'm here. You're not on your own. -> heard
  > @where I hear you. Where are you? -> heard

node heard public
  say Somebody. Somebody's there. Thank you. I'll keep the set on, and I'll call again at dusk, the same time every day, if you'll listen.
  do cset:opening.answered=1
  > @dusk I'll listen at dusk. -> hub

conv opening.tend_fever
for opening
when cflag:opening.step=2 & cflag:opening.task=3 & cflag:opening.tended=0
topic "Let me see to the boy."
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say He's through there, on the kitchen floor. He won't take water from me any more.
  > @treat Show me. I'll see what I've got. -> treated
  > @later In a minute. Keep him cool. -> hub

node treated
  say You knelt down like it was a waiting room and not my kitchen. Go on. I'll hold his hand.
  do cset:opening.tended=1
  > @on Stay with him. I'll be quick. -> hub

conv opening.tend_cut
for opening
when cflag:opening.step=2 & cflag:opening.task=2 & cflag:opening.tended=0
topic "Let me look at that hand."
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say It's nothing. It's hot and it throbs and it's nothing.
  > @look Hold still. Let me dress it. -> dressed
  > @later Keep it up. I'll come back to it. -> hub

node dressed
  say Mind the edge. There. You always did hold on harder than you needed to.
  do cset:opening.tended=1
  > @ok Nearly done. -> hub

conv opening.tend_clock
for opening
when cflag:opening.step=2 & cflag:opening.task=13 & cflag:opening.tended=0
topic "I have the antidote. Let me in."
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say He's sat against the wall. He keeps saying he's fine. He isn't.
  > @give Roll his sleeve up. Now. -> given
  > @later Keep him talking. I'm getting it out. -> hub

node given
  say He didn't even flinch. Just closed his eyes. Is that good?
  do cset:opening.tended=1
  > @wait Give it a moment. -> hub

conv opening.tend_clock_med
for opening
when cflag:opening.step=2 & cflag:opening.task=14 & cflag:opening.tended=0
topic "I can keep him going. Let me."
prio quest
voice plain

node start
  say There's nothing that fixes it. I know. Just tell me there's something that slows it.
  > @bind Clean it and bind it. That buys time. -> bound
  > @later Keep him still. I'll be back. -> hub

node bound
  say Tight as that? All right. All right. I'll watch him.
  do cset:opening.tended=1
  > @ok Watch his colour. -> hub
